{"cuisine/meitei-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/meitei-cuisine","n":"Meitei cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Manipuri cuisine","cuisine/manipuri-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in India","intro":[["The Meitei people, also known as Meetei people, are a Tibeto-Burman ethnic group native to the Indian State of  Manipur. They form the largest and dominant ethnic group of Manipur in Northeast India. They speak the Meitei language (officially called Manipuri), one of the 22 official languages of the Republic of India and the sole official language of government of Manipur. The Meiteis primarily settle in the Imphal Valley region of modern-day Manipur, though a sizeable population has settled in the other Indian states of Assam, Tripura, Nagaland, Meghalaya, and Mizoram. There is also a notable presence of Meiteis in the neighbouring countries of Myanmar and Bangladesh. The Meiteis represent about 53% of Manipur's population, according to the 2011 census."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"meitei-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meitei_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Lukthel","ref":"site/lukthel-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"lukthel.com","note":"Meetei-origin category on a Manipuri recipe site.","url":"https://lukthel.com/recipe/category/origin/meetei","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Manipuri cuisine","cuisine/manipuri-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine"},"dish/brasserie-julien":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/brasserie-julien","n":"Brasserie Julien","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Brasserie Julien was a brasserie-style French cuisine restaurant located at 1422 Third Avenue  (between East 80th Street and East 81st Street) on the Upper East Side of Manhattan in New York City, as well as a jazz club. The establishment closed at the end of 2012."]],"src":"wikipedia"