gondi-food":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/gondi-food","n":"Gondi (food)","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#a99fb5","intro":[["Gondi, sometimes spelled gundi, is a Persian Jewish dish of meatballs made from ground lamb, veal or chicken traditionally served on Shabbat. Dried lime is sometimes used as an ingredient. Gondi are served as part of chicken soup on Shabbat and other Jewish holidays, like the similar-looking but unrelated Ashkenazi Jewish matzo balls."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-gondi-food"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gondi_(food)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Jewish cuisine","cuisine/jewish-cuisine"],["Mizrahi Jewish cuisine","cuisine/mizrahi-jewish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":10,"links":[["Besan","ingredient/besan"],["Cardamom","ingredient/cardamom"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Chickpea flour","ingredient/chickpea-flour"],["Dried lime","ingredient/dried-lime"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Ground turkey","ingredient/ground-turkey"],["Lamb","ingredient/lamb"],["Meatball","ingredient/meatball"],["Onions","ingredient/onions"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Tori Avey: Jewish Recipes","ref":"site/toriavey-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"toriavey.com","note":"Tori Avey's Jewish recipe index, often paired with notes on each dish's history.","url":"https://toriavey.com/jewish-recipes/","suggested":true},{"name":"The Nosher (My Jewish Learning)","ref":"site/myjewishlearning-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"myjewishlearning.com","note":"Recipe section of the nonprofit My Jewish Learning, covering Ashkenazi, Sephardi and Mizrahi home cooking and holiday food.","url":"https://www.myjewishlearning.com/recipes/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Jewish cuisine","links":[["Appetizing store","dish/appetizing-store"],["Bagel","dish/bagel"],["Brent's Deli","dish/brent-s-deli"],["Brisket (Jewish dish)","dish